# The files of theorem-labs/rocq-linux-process-semantics that toolchain/checker.Dockerfile builds the model from: the
# opam package rocq-linux-process-semantics-core, which is the theory LinuxProcessSemantics, the proof library
# LinuxProcessSemantics.Common (theories/Common) that the same package installs, and the two tools it installs. The
# cut leaves out every other file, so that a change to one of them leaves the checker image as it is. They include the
# repository's two other opam packages, rocq-linux-process-semantics-examples (theories/Examples) and
# rocq-linux-process-semantics (which installs the other two), its tests, its CI and its other tools. The cut holds
# one README, theories/Common/README.md: a change to it changes the cut's hash, LPS_TREE_SHA256.
# One git pathspec per line, for
#   grep -v -e '^#' -e '^$' toolchain/lps-core.paths | xargs -d '\n' git -C <checkout> archive <commit> -- | tar -x -C <dir>
dune-project
dune
rocq-linux-process-semantics-core.opam
LICENSE
theories
:(exclude)theories/Examples
tools/elf_snapshot.py
tools/gen_fd_lemmas.py
